# The Dockerfile does `ADD . /app`, so anything sitting in the build tree is
# baked into the deployed image. The image built 2026-08-11 carried 22 stale
# .pyc files from a developer worktree's __pycache__ that the main checkout
# never had. They were harmless -- the matching sources were identical -- but
# bytecode from whichever tree a human happened to build in has no business
# in a release artifact, and it makes two images built from the same commit
# compare as different.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Never needed at runtime; keeps build context small and image provenance
# tied to the commit rather than to local checkout state.
.git/
.gitignore
.worktrees/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.egg-info/

# NOTE: .venv is deliberately NOT ignored here. The host checkout has one, so
# it is currently copied in and then reconciled by `uv sync --frozen --no-dev`.
# Excluding it is the upstream uv convention and would be faster and cleaner,
# but it changes what the builder actually resolves, so it wants its own
# verified change rather than riding along with a bytecode fix.
